.\" tvchat-backend(1) man page.
.TH TVCHAT-BACKEND 1 "October 2026" "tvchat 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tvchat\-backend \- the chat helper behind tvchat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tvchat\-backend
.RB [ \-\-debug " [" \fIFILE\fR ]]
.RB [ \-\-trace " [" \fIFILE\fR ]]
.B serve
.br
.B tvchat\-backend
.B irc\-tail
.RB [ \-\-raw ]
.I ACCOUNT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tvchat\-backend
holds every live chat connection (IRC and talk(1)) for
.BR tvchat (1).
It is a single Python 3 program, standard library only, with one
.B selectors
loop over its standard input, every socket and a timer heap.
.PP
.B serve
is how
.B tvchat
runs it: one request line in, one framed reply out
.RB ( "<status> <nbytes>" ,
a newline, then the body).
Status 0 is success, 1 a message for the user, 2 an internal error.
Verbs:
.BR accounts ,
.BR connect ,
.BR disconnect ,
.BR convs ,
.BR join ,
.BR part ,
.BR send ,
.BR history ,
.BR members ,
.BR mark\-read ,
.B events
.RI [ "\-\-after SEQ" ],
.BR ping ,
.BR quit .
.B send
takes the commands
.BR /me ,
.BR /join ,
.BR /part ,
.BR /msg ,
.BR /nick ,
.B /topic
and
.B /quote
.RB ( //
for a line starting with
.BR / );
a server conversation takes nothing else.
When
.B history \-\-before
reaches the start of what is kept and the server has IRCv3
.BR chathistory ,
it asks the server, answers status 1 saying so, and a
.B history
.I CONV
.B before
event follows; joining a channel asks for its latest 50 the same way
(event
.BR "history CONV latest" ).
.PP
A
.B protocol = talk
account is a client of chat-setup's talkd on the LAN master (\fBhost\fP,
\fBport\fP 518, \fBuser\fP, \fBtalk_view\fP classic | irc):
.B join
calls,
.B answer
.I CONV
answers a call,
.B part
hangs up or declines;
.B send
sends whole lines,
.B keys
.I CONV TEXT
keystrokes as typed (TEXT escaped as reply fields are).
Events:
.B talk
.I CONV STATE DETAIL
(calling, ringing, incoming, connected, ended) and
.B typing
.I CONV TEXT
(the other side's unfinished line).
.PP
A quiet IRC server gets a PING after 90 s, and the connection is dead
after 30 s more with no answer.
A connection that was up and is lost is made again after 2, 4, 8 ... up to
300 s (the account stays
.B connecting
meanwhile;
.B disconnect
stops it) and the open channels are joined again.
Once registered, lines go out in a burst of 5, then one every 0.5 s;
PONG and QUIT go first.
.PP
Replies are TAB-separated lines; inside a field TAB, newline, CR and
backslash are written
.BR \et ", " \en ", " \er ", " \e\e .
Nothing terminal-specific ever appears in a reply.
.PP
.B irc\-tail
.I ACCOUNT
connects one account in the terminal and prints its events
.RB ( \-\-raw :
every IRC line too); typed lines go to the newest channel,
.B /join #x
and
.B /quit
work.
For checking an account by hand.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/tvchat/tvchat.conf
.RB ( $TVCHAT_CONF
names another; the old
.I ~/.config/tvmail/tvchat.conf
is read when it is missing), INI syntax, no interpolation.
Write comments on lines of their own: a
.B #
after a value is part of the value.
.PP
.B [chat]
.B autoconnect =
.I name, ...
connects those accounts when
.B serve
starts.
.PP
.BI [account: NAME ]
\(em
.B protocol = irc
(or
.BR deltachat ,
not supported yet),
.BR display ,
.BR host ,
.B port
(6697, or 6667 with
.BR "tls = false" ),
.BR tls ,
.B verify
(default true),
.B cafile
(a full path: no
.B ~
expansion),
.BR nick ,
.BR realname ,
.B sasl
(the SASL login; leave it out to connect unauthenticated),
.B channels
(comma-separated).
.SH PASSWORDS
Never in the configuration file.
For an account with
.BR sasl ,
in this order, and in each place only an entry for that login counts:
.B $TVCHAT_PASS_\fIACCOUNT\fR
(e.g.
.BR $TVCHAT_PASS_LIBERA ),
then
.I ~/.mu-tickets
.RB ( irc://\fIlogin\fB:\fIpassword\fB@\fIhost\fR ,
or a
.B *://
entry; the file is
.B $TVMAIL_MU_TICKETS
if set), then
.I ~/.netrc
.RB ( "machine \fIhost\fB login \fIlogin\fB password \fIpassword\fR" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-debug " [FILE]
log every serve request, every IRC line in and out (SASL payloads
redacted), the TLS version and cipher, and why a connection ended
(default:
.IR debug.tvchat.backend.log ).
.TP
.BI "\-\-trace " [FILE]
write cProfile data on exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tvchat (1),
.BR tvmail\-backend (1)
